module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_dormant_runner_tree_is_activated_on_a_deprecated_runner_version

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CeilingNotStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }
import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }

// A RUNNER TREE IS NOT A THING THAT GETS CHECKED WHEN IT WAKES UP. The fleet judges a tree's release
// while it is converging it -- gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge runner_slot_tree_held counts a tree
// as held only when its listener is the release the fleet pins -- and that judgement is built from the
// committed population (runner_slot_tree_targets_of maps desired_runner_slot_members). A tree that has
// been sitting installed-but-never-activated is in no committed population, so nothing reads its
// release, and the moment an operator unmasks and starts it they are starting a listener GitHub has
// deprecated. The JIT registration carries DisableUpdate = True (extdeps.github.actions_runner), so the
// listener will not fix itself either.
data a_dormant_runner_tree_is_activated_on_a_deprecated_runner_version: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_dormant_runner_tree_is_activated_on_a_deprecated_runner_version" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: CeilingNotStated },
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an installed runner tree that was never activated keeps the Actions Runner release it was extracted with, because the provisioner extracts only for a slot it is ADDING (gunbc.runner.runner_slot_provision runner_slot_provision_plan_over: MemberChanged emits nothing) and a JIT-registered listener never updates itself (extdeps.github.actions_runner: the JIT settings carry DisableUpdate = True). Activation -- unmask, enable, start -- is the one moment the tree's release meets the fleet, and it is the moment no modeled route reads it.",
    "HARM: capacity that is not capacity. A deprecated listener registers, is told it 'cannot receive messages', and its service loop re-registers on a timer (observed at roughly one attempt every five seconds) while the host presents as enrolled: unit active, registration present, jobs never assigned. The operator repairs it by hand -- copying bin/ and externals/ from a current tree -- which is exactly the work the tree-install route exists to make unnecessary, and the failure is invisible to any capacity read that counts active units. A deprecated listener that GitHub DOES still assign work to can also die mid-job.",
    "SPECIMEN (srv1, 2026-11-09, hand activation by bold-wren-111 under the operator's 'yes please do A and then B'): srv1-07, srv1-08 and srv1-09 were unmasked, enabled and started as CI runners from the shared template (labels self-hosted,linux,arm64,gunbc-heavy,srv1). All three trees were on runner 2.336.0, which GitHub had deprecated, while the fleet's live tree (srv1-01) and the pinned artifact (gunbc.runner.runner_slot_provision fleet_runner_slot_artifact, and gunbc.runner.runner_lifecycle actions_runner_release_2_338_2) were on 2.338.2. Each unit looped re-registering every ~5s until stopped; the repair was an rsync of bin/ and externals/ from srv1-01. srv1-03 through srv1-06 have no install trees at all, so the same activation route applied to them would have failed differently -- absent, not stale.",
    "WHERE THE MODEL SHOULD HAVE CAUGHT IT, and did not: the tree route already exists and already carries the right judgement -- gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge runner_host_file_converge_ci_wet converges each slot's tree through RunnerSlotTreeStanding, whose arms read owner, mode AND listener release (RunnerSlotTreeHeld, RunnerSlotTreeRebuilt for a tree the converge rebuilt onto the pinned release), and whose own header says that with the version pin moved, 'applying this converge is the whole upgrade'. The judgement is built from runner_slot_tree_targets_of(deploy), which maps desired_runner_slot_members -- 'the slots whose trees are judged are exactly the desired slots the actuation phase activates'. A dormant tree is outside that scope BY DEFINITION: it is dormant because it was never in the committed population, so the converge never reads its release, and the operator's unmask/enable/start meets a deprecated listener with nothing in between. The shape of the fix is to key the same judgement on the UNIT BEING STARTED rather than on the population being converged, so activation of any tree, committed or not, is refused when its listener is not the pinned release.",
    "THE SAME SCOPING IS WHY THE FIX IS CHEAP FOR THE SLOTS THAT SHOULD HAVE HAD TREES: because the converge's subject list IS the derived population, a slot that the derivation commits is converged automatically -- srv1-03 through srv1-06, absent today, receive a tree from the pinned artifact the moment they become desired members, with no new route. The half of this failure mode that no route covers is the slot that is started WITHOUT being desired; that is the activation-time reading named above, and it is the frontier.",
    "CURRENT RUNG: detected, unmitigated. No modeled route reads a dormant tree's release before it is started; the hand activation above is the specimen and was repaired by hand. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: an activation route (unmask/enable/start of a slot unit) that reads the tree's release against the fleet pin and refuses before starting, at which point the residual is only the window between that reading and the start. RESIDUAL today: an operator with root can start any tree, and nothing in the model can see the tree until something asks the host -- which is the same reading-shape recorded at gunbc.recurring_failure_mode absent_reads_identically_to_never_looked.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    decl_ref("gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge", "runner_slot_tree_held"),
    decl_ref("gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge", "RunnerSlotTreeHeld"),
    decl_ref("gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge", "RunnerSlotTreeRebuilt"),
    decl_ref("gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge", "runner_slot_tree_targets_of"),
    decl_ref("gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge", "runner_host_file_converge_ci_wet"),
    decl_ref("gunbc.runner.runner_slot_provision", "fleet_runner_slot_artifact"),
    decl_ref("gunbc.runner.runner_lifecycle", "actions_runner_release_2_338_2"),
  ],
}
